    "evidence": "composed",
    "note": "Built from webhook-comment-created.json (itself composed from the documented envelope) for S-26.6's self-service link code. The webhooks page says the comment \"is the same shape returned from the Jira REST API when a comment is retrieved\", and the REST comment (swagger-v3, getComment) carries `author`, `updateAuthor`, `created` and `updated`; this file is the *Edit All Comments* case of TD-031's 2026-11-06 amendment item 9: another account (PM Two, who holds the permission) edited Dev One's comment to put a code into it, so `author` stays Dev One, `updateAuthor` is PM Two and `updated` is two minutes after `created`. The contract test patches `updated` back to `created` in one case so the `updateAuthor` check is seen alone. Jira announces an edit as `comment_updated`, which this normaliser ignores, so a delivery of exactly this shape — a `comment_created` whose comment already carries an edit — is not what a site sends; the shape a person meets is the REST thread read (*I wrote it on …*, `getComments`), which answers an edited comment with these same fields. The webhook test uses it to show the claim builder refuses the shape wherever it arrives."
  },
